{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Capstone 04 \u2014 Multimodal Document QA (Vision-First PDF, Tables, Charts) Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. **Ingest.** Walk a corpus of 10k PDF pages across 10-Ks, scientific papers, and scanned documents. Render each page to a 1536x2048 PNG. Persist `{doc_id, page_num, image_path}`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. **Embed.** Run ColQwen2.5-v0.2 on each page image. Output shape ~2048 patch embeddings of dim 128. Apply DocPruner to keep the highest-signal half. Write to Vespa multi-vector field or Qdrant multi-vector."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3. **Query.** For each incoming query, embed with the query tower (token-level embeddings). Run MaxSim against the index: for every query token, take the max dot-product over page patch embeddings, sum. Return top-k pages."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "4. **Synthesize.** Call Qwen3-VL-30B with the query and the top-5 page images. Prompt: \"Answer using only the supplied pages. Cite each claim by (doc_id, page) and name the region (figure, table, paragraph).\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "5. **Evidence regions.** Post-process the answer to extract cited regions. If the VLM emits bounding boxes (Qwen3-VL does), render them as overlays in the viewer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "6. **OCR fallback.** For pages identified as equation-dense (heuristic on image variance), run Nougat or dots.ocr and pass the OCR text as an extra channel alongside the image."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "7. **Eval.** Run ViDoRe v3 (retrieval nDCG@5) and M3DocVQA (multi-page QA accuracy). Also run OCR-then-text pipeline on the same corpus with the same synthesizer. Produce a content-type \u00d7 approach matrix."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "8. **UI.** Streamlit prototype first; Next.js 15 production viewer with page-by-page evidence-region overlay."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Measure ColQwen2.5-v0.2 vs ColQwen3-omni on the same corpus. Which pages does one get right and the other miss? Add a \"content class\" tag to the index to route by type.\n\n2. Prune embeddings aggressively (75%, 90%). Find the compression cliff: the point where ViDoRe nDCG@5 drops below the OCR baseline.\n\n3. Build a hybrid: run OCR-then-text and ColQwen in parallel, fuse with RRF, rerank with a cross-encoder. Does the hybrid beat either alone? Where does it help most?\n\n4. Swap Qwen3-VL-30B for a smaller VLM (Qwen2.5-VL-7B). Measure the accuracy-per-dollar curve.\n\n5. Add handwritten-note support. Render the handwriting corpus, embed with ColQwen, measure retrieval. Compare against a handwriting OCR pipeline."
      ]
    }
  ],
